                        "entry_id": "d8f42f14-62a3-3ae3-b2e7-3396069ebb2b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A shining quality; brilliance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "12f63233-cc8d-40a6-bfb0-16baf9285651",
                                "sense_id": "e11ca006-cb81-3ae0-9246-58df5adeb784",
                                "text": "[…] to assist greatly in the consumption of the lamp, and to diminish the aqueous precipitations produced on the interior of the lantern glass, which has the effect of reducing more or less the brilliancy of the light."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "047d7091-35ad-458b-94fe-fdb0eef38381",
                                "sense_id": "e11ca006-cb81-3ae0-9246-58df5adeb784",
                                "text": "[H]is ideal of grandeur was a splendid façade, diffusing its brilliancy outward too, irradiating hospitality."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4e3c60f6-5dbd-3e54-9b55-bcfe1014fa23",
                        "entry_id": "d8f42f14-62a3-3ae3-b2e7-3396069ebb2b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An act of being brilliant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee7f648f-8e71-4362-80c9-b0effa11cada",
                                "sense_id": "4e3c60f6-5dbd-3e54-9b55-bcfe1014fa23",
                                "text": "His brilliancy lay in combining old concepts from far-flung fields into a new idea."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d08f713f-0f7a-41fc-b158-cac8dbfaec71",
                                "sense_id": "4e3c60f6-5dbd-3e54-9b55-bcfe1014fa23",
                                "text": "Surely it must have been his brilliancy that accounted for Vardon standing out as a stroke or two better than such a model of steadiness as J. H. Taylor[.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c118200-e9ea-4753-bb2a-15f22cd3630c",
                                "sense_id": "4e3c60f6-5dbd-3e54-9b55-bcfe1014fa23",
                                "text": "2013, Hannah Eichler, The Key to Brilliancy: How to Unlock Your Child's Genius"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "28f785f2-99b1-3d61-9617-6c17d0b92901",
                        "entry_id": "d8f42f14-62a3-3ae3-b2e7-3396069ebb2b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A spectacular and beautiful game of chess, generally featuring sacrificial attacks and unexpected moves."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90ec7693-965b-4632-a3d6-873dc30c4530",
                                "sense_id": "28f785f2-99b1-3d61-9617-6c17d0b92901",
                                "text": "Bobby Fischer, one of the greatest chess players who ever lived, died at the age of sixty-four from kidney failure. He had lived one year for each square on a chessboard. / THE GOOD / First of all, you should learn the term “brilliancy.” It refers to a game that is played with spectacular strategy and beauty, typically featuring unexpected moves and ingenious ideas. In other words, the game is extraordinary! At age thirteen, Bobby Fischer won a brilliancy against twenty-six-year-old Donald Byrne."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ffe032f6-f26c-48dc-b5d9-5e0f6d7b73db",
                        "source_entry_id": "d8f42f14-62a3-3ae3-b2e7-3396069ebb2b",
                        "source_sense_description": "shining quality",
                        "target_lang_word": "brillance",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brillance",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a47aae0c-d7c2-3b1e-a708-274386b16231",
                                        "entry_id": "489f369a-4d2d-3b3b-b175-0d6d097676d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "État de ce qui est brillant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d3fc02f-0057-4cff-9c7a-6a6b25cc0934",
                                                "sense_id": "a47aae0c-d7c2-3b1e-a708-274386b16231",
                                                "text": "À quatre heures exactement, elle arriva. Ce ne fut d’abord qu’un éclat de brillance dans le fond de la rue comme l’éclair avant le tonnerre. Puis sa carrosserie noire à angles droits, sérieuse et luxueuse, emplit l’espace entre les maisons. Elle s’avançait, lente et silencieuse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa9abd10-e114-4c14-8998-d57dee60720e",
                                                "sense_id": "a47aae0c-d7c2-3b1e-a708-274386b16231",
                                                "text": "La mari, le jeudi, garnit le trottoir, sa sœur déambule dans sa robe de soie violette et fait jaillir, à chaque pas, les brèves brillances des perles de la bourse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "900671b6-8c51-4142-bdbc-d7f5a6c1bd54",
                                                "sense_id": "a47aae0c-d7c2-3b1e-a708-274386b16231",
                                                "text": "Ce type de spectrophotomètre est muni d’une ouverture ajustable qui permet la mesure de la brillance des échantillons en incluant ou excluant la composante spéculaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58d37bc5-fbc6-494c-8cce-b7ed495492de",
                                                "sense_id": "a47aae0c-d7c2-3b1e-a708-274386b16231",
                                                "text": "Pas plus que les autres elle ne saurait dire comment on la voit, souhaitant par-dessus tout ne pas être vue, faisant plutôt partie des ignorées, des bonnes élèves sans brillance et sans repartie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
